# Line endings: LF in the repository AND in every working copy, whatever the
# machine's core.autocrlf says. Before this, core.autocrlf=true checked text
# out as CRLF (locally and on the Windows CI runner) while tools that rewrite
# files wrote LF, so a test reading its own sources could pass here and fail
# on CI (PR #10). Everything we run reads LF: rustc, node, PowerShell 5.1,
# NSIS, cscript.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files are the one thing cmd.exe needs CRLF for (none yet).
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary: never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.webp binary
*.wav binary
*.mp3 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.exe binary
*.msi binary
*.dll binary
*.zip binary
*.docx binary

docs/** linguist-documentation
